resources.string:
Gold nuclei are hidden in the chamber, like in the experiment that revealed the atomic nucleus in 1909. Tap a detector on the edge to fire an alpha particle from it, and see where it ends up:

• a struck-out dot: it hit a nucleus head-on and was absorbed;
• a U-turn arrow: it came back, because two nuclei grazed its path at once, or one grazed its entry point;
• a number: it came out at the other detector bearing the same number. A nucleus that grazes its path diagonally deflects it by a quarter turn.

Tap inside the chamber to place or remove a nucleus. When all are placed, Check reveals the real ones.
